      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.74,
            0.047,
            0.862,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": "Quadrilaterals"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.203,
            0.085,
            0.847,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "(ii) A quadrilateral having three right angles must be a rectangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.11,
            0.848,
            0.15
          ],
          "content": "(iii) A quadrilateral whose diagonals bisect each other must be a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.153,
            0.848,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": "(iv) A quadrilateral whose diagonals are perpendicular to each other must be a rhombus."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.195,
            0.849,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "(v) A quadrilateral in which the opposite angles are equal must be a parallelogram."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.237,
            0.848,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": "(vi) A quadrilateral in which all the angles are equal is a rectangle."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.262,
            0.648,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "(vii) Isosceles trapeziums are parallelograms."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.337,
            0.591,
            0.363
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "SUMMARY"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.378,
            0.806,
            0.424
          ],
          "content": "A **rectangle** is a quadrilateral in which the angles are all 90°. Properties of a rectangle"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.427,
            0.641,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": "y Opposite sides of a rectangle are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.452,
            0.792,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": "y Opposite sides of a rectangle are parallel to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.475,
            0.823,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": "Diagonals of a rectangle are of equal length and they bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.518,
            0.823,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": "A **square** is a quadrilateral in which all the angles are 90°, and all the sides are of equal length."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.561,
            0.474,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "**Properties of a square —**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.585,
            0.806,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "y The opposite sides of a square are parallel to each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.609,
            0.823,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": "The diagonals of a square are of equal lengths and they bisect each other at 90°."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.651,
            0.813,
            0.673
          ],
          "content": "y The diagonals of a square bisect the angles of the square."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.675,
            0.823,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "A **parallelogram** is a quadrilateral in which opposite sides are parallel."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.213,
            0.718,
            0.551,
            0.739
          ],
          "content": "**Properties of a parallelogram —**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.742,
            0.724,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": "The opposite sides of a parallelogram are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.236,
            0.766,
            0.822,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": "In a parallelogram, the adjacent angles add up to 180°, and the opposite angles are equal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.808,
            0.755,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": "y The diagonals of a parallelogram bisect each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.832,
            0.823,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "A **rhombus** is a quadrilateral in which all the sides have the same length."
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.872,
            0.915,
            0.918,
            0.936
          ],
          "content": "109"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
